wart@cco.caltech.edu (Michael L. Thomas) writes:

>my ghost started attacking me in the shop.  No biggie, except that the
>shopkeeper apparently didn't think I was dead and also started attacking
>me.  So I'm standing in the door with a ghost and a shopkeeper hitting me.
>Why??  How can I avoid this?  Would the same thing happen if it had been
>someone else's ghost?

You guessed it. The shopkeeper in the bones file still remembers the name
of the player who robbed his shop. If you had been using another name, the
shopkeeper wouldn't have been angry to you, he would have just said
"Hello A, I'm looking for B" (where A is your name now, and B is the name
of the player who robbed the shop). And I believe this happens in every
version of hack/nethack.

>Also, every ghost level that I come across seems to be my own.  Do ghost
>levels "expire" after a while, so that the most recently created ghosts
>are more likely to be found than the ones who died 2 years ago?

As far as I know, it's not like that. The game doesn't care about the date
of the bones files, they just have 1/3 chance of popping up whenever the
game creates that level. It's just that usually this happens before the
2 years are gone..
